## Key Features
# 1. Simplified Model Management: KAITO manages large model files using container images and provides an OpenAI-compatible server for inference calls.
# 2. Automated GPU node provisioning and configuration : KAITO automatically provisions GPU nodes based on model requirements and bootstraps GPU node setup and inference service deployment behind the scenes using simple YAML configurations. Kaito will automatically provision and configure GPU nodes for you. This can help reduce the operational burden of managing GPU nodes, configuring them for Kubernetes, and tuning model deployment parameters to fit GPU profiles.
# 3. Advanced Fine-Tuning Capabilities: The platform streamlines parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT) methods on Kubernetes, including low-rank adaptation (LoRA) and quantized low-rank adaptation (QLoRA) for efficient memory utilization.
# 4. Multiple Runtime Support: KAITO provides support for popular open-source inference runtimes including vLLM and transformers, offering flexibility in deployment options.
# 5. Architecture: KAITO follows the classic Kubernetes CRD/controller design pattern with major components including a workspace controller that reconciles custom resources and creates inference workloads, and a node provisioner controller that integrates with cloud APIs to add new GPU nodes to clusters. The system utilizes workspace custom resources to describe GPU requirements and inference specifications, enabling declarative AI model management at scale. KAITO will also offers RAG (Retrieval-augmented generation)
# 6. Reduced cost: Kaito can help you save money by splitting inferencing across lower end GPU nodes which may also be more readily available and cost less than high-end GPU nodes.
# 7. Support for popular open-source LLMs: Kaito offers preset configurations for popular open-source LLMs. This can help you deploy and manage open-source LLMs on AKS and integrate them with your intelligent applications.
# 8. Fine-grained control: You can have full control over data security and privacy, model development and configuration transparency, and the ability to fine-tune the model to fit your specific use case.
# 9. Network and data security: You can ensure these models are ring-fenced within your organization's network and/or ensure the data never leaves the Kubernetes cluster.


## KAITO Architecture Components
# 1. API Server: Manages KAITO custom resources and handles model deployment requests.
# 2. AI Workload Controller: Orchestrates the deployment and scaling of AI models based on workload requirements.
# 3. Node Provisioner: Automatically provisions appropriate GPU-enabled nodes for AI workloads.
# 4. Workspace Management: Provides isolated environments for different AI models and experiments.
# 5. Model Registry Integration: Connects to both public registries (like HuggingFace) and private model repositories.
# 6. GPU Node Management

## KAITO automatically handles GPU node provisioning and management:
# The system automatically:
# 1. Provisions GPU-enabled nodes when needed
# 2. Scales workloads based on demand
# 3. Manages model loading and caching
# 4. Provides HTTP endpoints for model inference
# You can install KAITO on AKS as add-on by using “ — enable-ai-toolchain-operator” flag on az cli command.

